**Motivation of change**

Previously NodeFieldDefinitionByName was returning `0, false` when field definition was not found, but `0` - is a valid ref

```go
func (d *Document) NodeFieldDefinitionByName(node Node, fieldName ByteSlice) (definition int, exists bool) {
	for _, i := range d.NodeFieldDefinitions(node) {
		if bytes.Equal(d.Input.ByteSlice(d.FieldDefinitions[i].Name), fieldName) {
			return i, true
		}
	}
	return
}
```

Method `FieldDefinition` was not checking value of `exists` return param of  `ast.NodeFieldDefinitionByName` and as `0 != -1` always `true` in such case we were returning `0, true` - which is incorrect behaviour
```go
func (w *Walker) FieldDefinition(field int) (definition int, exists bool) {
	fieldName := w.document.FieldNameBytes(field)
	definition, _ = w.definition.NodeFieldDefinitionByName(w.EnclosingTypeDefinition, fieldName)
	exists = definition != -1
	return
}
```

Such behavior was allowing planner v1 to correctly plan `__typename` field, so to make it work again it requires an ugly fix

